Subject: [PATCH 4/4] binder: support multiple /dev instances

Android 8 split binder into three domains -- /dev/binder, /dev/hwbinder and
/dev/vndbinder -- and this kernel registers exactly one. drivers/android/binder.c
has a single misc_register(&binder_miscdev) named "binder", and there is no
CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_DEVICES. Without the other two, hwservicemanager has
nothing to open, and HIDL is how Android 9 reaches every HAL.

This is not a configuration switch: the context manager state
(binder_context_mgr_node, binder_context_mgr_uid) is file-scope global here and
has to become per-device.

Rather than write that by hand on an IPC driver, this is Google's own backport,
taken from the deprecated/android-3.10 branch of kernel/common -- the same
kernel version this tablet runs -- as three commits applied in order:

  1c5b844  android: binder: support multiple context managers.
  9cf47e4  android: binder: deal with contexts in debugfs.
  059e115  android: binder: support multiple /dev instances.

30 of the 31 hunks applied as they came. The one that did not is in
binder_ioctl_set_ctx_mgr(), and the reason is instructive: upstream calls
security_binder_set_context_mgr() there, and this Qualcomm CAF tree does not, so
the hunk's leading context did not match. Its substance -- replacing the two
globals with context-> members -- was applied by hand, and nothing else in that
function was touched.

The defconfig sets CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_DEVICES="binder,hwbinder,vndbinder".
The Kconfig default stays "binder", so this changes nothing for anyone who does
not ask for it.

Verifiable without a ROM: boot the recovery and look for the three nodes in
/dev.
